rker is\n77\t    # the synthetic genesis entry written as line 1 of every rotation-\n78\t    # created fresh audit-log.jsonl. Per ADR-055-AMEND-2 (drafted in\n79\t    # this plan): verifier reads `audit-log.rotation-manifest.json`\n80\t    # sidecar; if present, line 1 of fresh log MUST be a\n81\t    # chain_reset_marker entry — non-marker line 1 = STATUS_TAMPER.\n82\t    # Registered via kernel-override\n83\t    # PLAN-112-FOLLOWUP-WAVE-B3-AUDIT-EMIT-EXTENSION at v1.39.4.\n84\t    \"chain_reset_marker\",\n85\t    # PLAN-118 AC-B5 — closed-enum producer-pollution forensic breadcrumb.\n86\t    # Emitted by chokepoint 1 (audit_emit._emit_chain_reset_marker_under_lock)\n87\t    # + chokepoint 4 (spool_writer._phase4_build_batch) when the canonical-\n88\t    # resolution check (audit_hmac._ensure_canonical_lib_modules) detects\n89\t    # a stale `_lib` copy on sys.path. Allowlist payload: chokepoint\n90\t    # (enum: chain_reset_marker | spool_drain) + reason_code (enum:\n91\t    # audit_emit_path_pollution | canonical_json_path_pollution |\n92\t    # audit_hmac_path_pollution) + path_sha256_prefix (8 hex chars) +\n93\t    # expected_canonical_prefix (8 hex chars). NO `__file__` raw echo\n94\t    # per [[feedback-closed-enum-breadcrumb-must-not-echo-rejected-value]].\n95\t    \"audit_producer_path_pollution_detected\",\n96\t    # PLAN-125 WS-1 (kooky-harvest) — per-tool-call lifecycle telemetry.\n97\t    # Deny-by-default: routes through the dedicated _scrub_ branch +\n98\t    # _TOOL_CALL_LIFECYCLE_RECORDED_ALLOWLIST below, NEVER\n99\t    # _EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH (Sec MF-SEC-2). Carries ONLY 4 closed fields:\n100\t    # tool_name_enum (mcp__* → mcp_other, Sec MF-SEC-1), duration_bucket"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ad11fd4-f4ee-435e-bb65-ad9fa0e55842","uuid":"e68095ca-3239-4d23-9b5c-8c62d292a257","timestamp":"2026-11-15T10:13:02.330Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repa