{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4YE7J4tv7jV37obiMxD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found no P0 and no P1 in this payload. Condition 7 (hooks become thin entry points over `_lib` modules) holds for this file, and so does the part of condition 5 that puts the new package under the kernel. There are four P2 follow-ups, listed below.\n\nOne limit: the base `audit_emit.py` isn't in the read-only tree, and this payload only shows the start of its diff. So I compared the new code against the removed text visible here plus counts and spot checks. It is not a byte-by-byte match against the whole old file, and I could not run the tests.\n\n**What the payload does.** `.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py` is now a short facade. It keeps the imports, the `_KNOWN_ACTIONS` list, `iter_events` and `emit_credential_rotation_due`. Everything else comes from 33 modules under `.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/`. `install()` in that package's `__init__.py` re-binds each function to the facade's namespace.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- **Action list:** `_KNOWN_ACTIONS` at `audit_emit.py:45-377` has 331 unique entries. That matches the old count recorded in the removed comments (327→330, plus `session_memory_delta_observed`). No installed part overrides it; only `actions.py` exports that name, and it is never installed.\n- **Pass-through list:** `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH` (`federation_schemas.py:214-399`) matches the old region visible in the diff, including the \"MOVED/REMOVED from passthrough\" notes. Actions with their own field filter stay out of it.\n- **Dispatch:**\n  - The 5 dispatch groups have 173 per-action branches, and each ends in `return True`.\n  - Branches that drop a malformed event return `None`, so nothing is written, as in the old chain. Each group ends with `return False`.\n  - The final default writes only the action name. Unknown actions are dropped with a log line.\n  - The reserved federation and `execution_context` actions keep their branches.\n- **Fail-open:** the writing code in `writer.py` is unchanged text. The old `emit_generic` branches sat at function level with no top-level `try`, so moving them adds no fail-open or fail-closed inversion.\n- **Moved-code risks:**\n  - The parts have no decorators, classes, nested functions or lambdas. Every re-bound function therefore looks names up in the facade, so test patch points such as `audit_emit._log_path` still work. `global _FALLBACK_NOTIFIED` writes to the facade.\n  - `deepcopy` only copies sets, dicts, ints and compiled regexes.\n  - `iter_events` is rebound once `install()` has run.\n  - The typing names dropped from the facade imports only appear in annotations, and `from __future__ import annotations` keeps those as strings.\n  - Spool-writer setup is still at the end of the file (the old file had `install_exit_handlers` at line 13344, per a PLAN-194 note).\n- **Public names:** every name callers use resolves to a part's `__all__` or the facade. The four that don't (`_memoize_path`, `_validate_dispatch_archetype_hint`, `edge_trigger_should_emit`, `emit_federation_key_floor_rejected`) appear only in comments or docstrings.\n- **Adopters:**\n  - `install.sh` copies each `_lib` entry recursively (`scripts/install.sh:1524-1541`). The exclusion list (`scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:95-107`) does not skip `_audit_emit_parts`, so it reaches adopters.\n  - `check-audit-registry-coverage.py` still finds the `_KNOWN_ACTIONS` literal in the facade.\n  - `check_arbitration_kernel.py:312` covers `_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*`, matching condition 5.\n- **Python:** I found no syntax or APIs newer than 3.9, and only standard-library imports (`copy`, `importlib`, `types`, `re`, `time`, `hashlib`).\n\n**NEW FINDINGS (annex):** none.\n\n**P2 follow-ups:**\n1. **Unused duplicate action list.** `.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/actions.py`, `actions_core.py` and `actions_extended.py` are not in the install list at `audit_emit.py:415-452` and nothing imports them. They still hold a second copy of the action list (234 + 97 = 331 entries), with all the per-action history comments the live copy lost.\n   - Scenario: a maintainer adds a new action to `actions_core.py`, where the documentation now lives. The live list is unchanged, so `_write_event` (`writer.py:558-560`) drops the event as unknown and only logs a line.\n   - The files ship to adopters and sit under the kernel paths. The `actions.py` docstring calls them exported by the facade, and `actions_extended.py:1` names a `schemas_actions` module that doesn't exist.\n   - Fix: delete the three files, or build the facade's list from them and add a test that the two are equal.\n2. **Code that exists only for source-scanning checks.**\n   - `audit_emit.py:473-480`: `emit_generic` has two branches identical to its fallthrough.\n   - `audit_emit.py:21`, `382-383` and `455-461`: the replay part is imported as `_streaming`, and `iter_events` is defined twice.\n   - These seem to exist so that checks like `check-audit-read-api-stable.py` (which reads top-level `def` names) still pass. Behaviour is the same, but those checks now inspect stand-ins rather than the real code.\n   - Fix: add a comment saying why, or make the checks follow the install list.\n3. **Documentation dropped.** The module docstring and its design rules (additive-only, fail-open, concurrent-write safe, redaction, stdlib-only) were removed from the facade and now appear nowhere in it. Fix: restore a short version.\n4. **Older bug, moved unchanged.** At `writer.py:758-761`, the `except (OSError, PermissionError)` branch calls `_write_fallback(line)`. If the error comes from `log.parent.mkdir` or opening the lock, `line` doesn't exist yet. The resulting `UnboundLocalError` is caught by the outer `except`, so the event is lost with only a log line, despite the `/tmp` fallback promise. Fix: build the fallback line from `event`, as the `FileLockTimeout` b