h a breadcrumb before any handler runs. Reserved federation and execution_context actions keep their branches.\\n- Fail-open: the old emit_generic branches sat at function level with no top-level try, so moving them adds no fail-open or fail-closed inversion. The writing code (writer.py) is the old text, re-indented.\\n- Moved-code risks: no decorators, classes, nested functions or lambdas in any part, so every rebound function looks names up in the facade. \\\"global _FALLBACK_NOTIFIED\\\" writes to the facade. deepcopy only handles frozensets, sets, dicts, ints and compiled regexes. Typing names dropped from the facade imports (List, Tuple, Callable, Iterator) appear only in annotations, which \\\"from __future__ import annotations\\\" keeps as strings, or in local annotations that are never evaluated. iter_events is rebound after install(). set_forensic_emitter and install_exit_handlers are still called at module end (the old file had install_exit_handlers at line 13344, per a PLAN-194 note).\\n- Public names: every audit_emit.<name> and \\\"from _lib.audit_emit import X\\\" used by non-test code resolves to a part's __all__ or the facade. The four unresolved names (_memoize_path, _validate_dispatch_archetype_hint, edge_trigger_should_emit, emit_federation_key_floor_rejected) appear only in comments or docstrings.\\n- Adopter delivery: install.sh copies each _lib entry recursively (scripts/install.sh:1524-1541), and _framework_path_excluded (scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:95-107) does not exclude _audit_emit_parts, so the package ships. check-audit-registry-coverage.py still finds the _KNOWN_ACTIONS literal in the facade.\\n- Python 3.9 / standard library only: no 3.10+ syntax or APIs found; imports limited to copy, importlib, types, re, time, hashlib.\\n\\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none.\\n\\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\\n1. P2 - .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/actions.py:1-16, actions_core.py, actions_extended.py:1. Never installed (absent from the roster at audit_emit.py:415-452) and imported nowhere, yet they hold a second 331-entry copy of the action list (234 + 97) carrying all the per-action provenance comments the live literal lost. Failure scenario: a maintainer registers a new action in actions_core.py, where the documentation now lives. The live _KNOWN_ACTIONS does not change, so _write_event (writer.py:558-560) drops the event as unknown with only a breadcrumb. The files ship to adopters and sit under the kernel paths. The actions.py docstring claims the facade exports them, and actions_extended.py:1 names a nonexistent \\\"schemas_actions\\\". Minimal fix: delete the three files, or build the facade's literal from them and add a test that the two sets are equal.\\n2. P2 - audit_emit.py:473-480, 21, 382-383, 455-461. emit_generic has two branches (tool_call_lifecycle_recorded, settings_tamper_detected) identical to its fallthrough. iter_events is defined twice, and the replay template is imported under the name _streaming. These appear to exist only so source-scanning checks (for example check-audit-read-api-stable.py, which reads top-level def names) keep passing. Behaviour is the same, but those checks now inspect stand-ins rather than the real code. Minimal fix: add a comment stating the purpose, or make the checks follow the install roster.\\n3. P2 - audit_emit.py:1. The module docstring and its design rules (additive-only, fail-open, concurrent-write safe, redaction, stdlib-only) were removed and now appear nowhere in the facade. Minimal fix: restore a short version of the docstring.\\n4. P2 (older defect, moved unchanged) - writer.py:758-761. In the \\\"except (OSError, PermissionError)\\\" branch, _write_fallback(line) references \\\"line\\\", which is unbound when the error comes from log.parent.mkdir or opening the FileLock. The resulting UnboundLocalError is caught by the outer except, so the event is lost with only a breadcrumb, contrary to the F-CHAOS-1 /tmp fallback promise. Minimal fix: serialize the fallback line from \\\"event\\\", as the FileLockTimeout branch at writer.py:750-756 already does.\",\"sentence\":\"This payload splits audit_emit.py into a facade over _lib/_audit_emit_parts that keeps the action list, field filters, pass-through set, default-deny, fail-open writer, patch points and Python 3.9 compatibility, as far as could be checked without the full base file, and it leaves no declared condition false and no P0, only P2 hygiene follow-ups.\"}","structured_output":{"decision":"GO","report":"SCOPE: payload 14/32 = first piece of the .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py diff. audit_emit.py becomes a facade (imports, _KNOWN_ACTIONS literal, iter_events, emit_credential_rotation_due) that binds 33 template modules under .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/ into its own namespace via _audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:install(). Limit: the base audit_emit.py is not in the read-only tree and this payload shows only the start of its diff. Equivalence was checked against the removed text visible here plus counts and spot checks, not byte-for-byte against the whole old file. Tests could not be run.\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS TOUCHED BY THIS PAYLOAD\n- Condition 7 (thin entry points over _lib modules; lookups stay on the facade): TRUE for this file. audit_emit.py:413-452 installs the parts. install() rebuilds each function with FunctionType(code, facade_globals, ...), so name lookups and test patch points (for example audit_emit._log_path) still resolve on the facade.\n- Condition 5 (kernel coverage of the split packages): TRUE for this package. check_arbitration_kernel.py:312 lists .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*.\n\nCHECKS PERFORMED (no defect found)\n- Action list: _KNOWN_ACTIONS at audit_emit.py:45-377 has 331 unique entries, matching the old count recorded in the removed comments (327->330 plus session_memory_delta_observed). No installed part overrides it; only actions.py exports that name, and it is not installed.\n- Pass-through list: _EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHRO